# A guard, not a build input. Nothing is meant to be built from this directory.
#
# Every image in this repository takes its own project directory as context --
# `forme/`, `suki/`, `tallow/`, `poketrack/` -- and each of those has its own
# .dockerignore that is the real one. This file exists for the mistake those
# cannot catch: running `docker build -f forme/frontend/Dockerfile .` from here,
# which the Dockerfile comments used to invite by saying "the repo root" back
# when that meant forme/.
#
# Without this, that command uploads all six projects as build context --
# including any untracked node_modules, which is over 100MB in plinth/ alone --
# and only then fails on a COPY that is not there. The failure is loud either
# way; this keeps it from being slow and from heating the daemon first.
*/node_modules
*/*/node_modules
*/.venv
*/*/.venv
*/dist
*/*/dist
*/build
*/*/build
*/.next
*/*/.next
.git
